scanner_errors=1 :: Requests: Foldkit: html element constructors must be called inside a runtime-driven render. The element was built outside a view, or foldkit was loaded as more than one instance (a bundler split foldkit and @foldkit/ui into separate copies).

## Reconciliation against evidence/logs/ui-dead-controls-inventory.md (53 dead instances / 19 routes)

The two counts measure different surfaces and are NOT expected to be equal; the ratchet pins the walker count.

1) Native <option> correction: the first walker version counted every <option> as a dead control, inflating the
   baseline to 119 (Index 15, RouterStrategy 15, RouterConfig 15, LearningDecisions 16, ...). A native option is
   owned by its select and is never independently wirable, so options are excluded and the select counts once:
   119 -> 40 dead controls. role=option on a non-option element (a custom row) still counts.
2) Human rows that are now wired (shared tree, S618 models wiring landed after the inventory was written):
   /models (2), /models/roles (11), /system/benchmark (4) -> walker reports 0 dead on Models, ModelsRoles, Benchmark;
   the human table rows for those routes are stale. That is ~13 of the 53 human instances, no longer dead.
3) Human-listed affordances that are not native controls: clickable model div rows, role-table rows, requests
   table rows, activity rows, and the llama-swap static 'click ...' text (~8 human instances). The walker counts
   controls a view actually renders (a/button/input/select/textarea + role-based controls), so rows without a
   role/tabindex are not machine-detectable and do not appear.
4) Scanner gap: Requests is recorded as an ERROR, not as zero controls. Its listbox calls foldkit's real
   childAttributes(), which needs a runtime render frame (src/ui/listbox.ts:54); the human inventory's ~9
   /requests controls therefore contribute 0 to the walker count.
5) Walker-only findings the human inventory missed or classified read-only: Observability refresh, StoreReceipts
   refresh, LocalLogs, SystemOperator 5, SystemExtensions 2, the second Operator-token input on LearningEvidence,
   the 'All roles' button on LocalLlamaSwapModels, and two extra Decisions selects (5 vs the human 3).
Net: 53 (human, source-level, includes affordances and pre-S618 routes) vs 40 (walker, native controls only,
excludes Requests). Difference = ~13 now-wired + ~8 non-control affordances + ~9 Requests gap (~30 human
instances) offset by ~11-15 walker-only findings.

